.SH NAME
lsvlan \- It lists the existing vlans for the cluster.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
\&\fBlsvlan\fR
.PP
\&\fBlsvlan\fR [\fIvlanid\fR]
.PP
\&\fBlsvlan\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR]
.PP
\&\fBlsvlan\fR [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
The \fBlsvlan\fR command lists all the vlans for the cluster. If \fIvlanid\fR is specifined it will list more details about this vlan including the nodes in the vlan.
.SH PARAMETERS
.IX Header "PARAMETERS"
\&\fIvlanid\fR is a unique vlan number. If it is omitted, all vlans will be listed.
.SH OPTIONS
.IX Header "OPTIONS"
.IP "\fB\-h|\-\-help\fR  Display usage message." 10
.IX Item "-h|--help Display usage message."
.PD 0
.IP "\fB\-v|\-\-version\fR  Command Version." 10
.IX Item "-v|--version Command Version."
.PD
.SH "RETURN VALUE"
.IX Header "RETURN VALUE"
0  The command completed successfully.
.PP
1  An error has occurred.
.SH EXAMPLES
.IX Header "EXAMPLES"
.IP "1. To list all the vlans in the cluster" 3
.IX Item "1. To list all the vlans in the cluster"
.Vb 1
\&  lsvlan
.Ve
.Sp
Output is similar to:
.Sp
.Vb 3
\&  vlan 3:
\&      subnet 10.3.0.0
\&      netmask 255.255.0.0
\&
\&  vlan 4:
\&      subnet 10.4.0.0
\&      netmask 255.255.0.0
.Ve
.IP "2. To list the details for vlan3" 3
.IX Item "2. To list the details for vlan3"
.Vb 1
\&  lsvlan 3
.Ve
.Sp
Output is similar to:
.Sp
.Vb 3
\&  vlan 3
\&      subnet 10.3.0.0
\&      netmask 255.255.0.0
\&
\&      hostname    ip address      node            vm host
\&      v3n1        10.3.0.1        c68m4hsp06
\&      v3n2        10.3.0.2        x3455n01
\&      v3n3        10.3.0.3        x3650n01
\&      v3n4        10.3.0.4        x3650n01kvm1    x3650n01
\&      v3n5        10.3.0.5        x3650n01kvm2    x3650n01
.Ve
.SH FILES
.IX Header "FILES"
/opt/xcat/bin/lsvlan
